  {"i":2106,"t":["greetings","culture"],"s":{"4":["festivals"]},"n":"お礼 (thanks) is greetings and 礼儀/bowing is culture; お礼 as a gift is festivals. 礼 alone rarely means 'ceremony', so sense 5 needs no entry."},
  {"i":2110,"t":["time"],"s":{},"n":"'One after another' is succession in time, not counting or ordinal order."},
  {"i":2118,"t":["qualities","transport"],"s":{},"n":"Single sense, so no sense entry. Priority and importance are qualities, and learners meet it constantly in 優先席 and right of way."},
  {"i":2129,"t":["movement"],"s":{"4":["relationships","feelings"],"6":["money"]},"n":"Floating is physical motion, not nature. クラスで浮く is mainly about getting on with others. 浮く for money left over is common. 'Merry' is rare."},
  {"i":2135,"t":["society","work","sports"],"s":{"2":["qualities"]},"n":"Delegates and representatives belong to society and work, and 日本代表 (national team) is a very common sports use. 'Typical' is qualities."},
  {"i":2159,"t":["qualities"],"s":{},"n":"Status quo is a state. The link to time is loose."},
  {"i":2195,"t":["actions"],"s":{},"n":"An adverb of manner (doing by force), not a degree or negation function word."}
